{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"P03|core0|lowering|semantic_projection|report\" docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md | head -80'","aggregated_output":"10:- **U1:** original user request on heterogeneous annual/interim reports, all\n58:| MC04 | Separate reported assertions, extraction readings, derivations, assumptions and conflicts. U1, U2, P, D. | Define source/derived/assumed status propagation and conflict handling; show both extraction error and a genuinely conflicting disclosure without silently changing either source. | Specified source/assumption constraints, review actions and conflict sets in Chs. 3, 6, 10. The 720-to-120 OCR repair differs from the 120-to-110 reported correction; transitive invalidation has a reference check. Bounded debt acceptance/source/assumption links are now checked; full workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\n59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\n68:| MC09 | Construct historical families through a specified method, with honest scope and search completeness. U2, U3, D. | Define candidate templates, model-sc